# CERT16c: a change to anything that can cause or steer a signature needs
# Bill's review before it reaches `main`. The `main` ruleset requires a
# code-owner review (approvals otherwise 0), so every other change keeps
# INTEGRATOR's merge-on-CI flow. Agents push as the aerocommons-agents App,
# which is not a bypass actor. See docs/signing_key.md, "Who can cause a
# signature".

# The signing workflows, and every other workflow (a new one could read the key).
/.github/workflows/            @billmallard
# The signer and the device's trusted key set (PUBLIC_KEYS).
/packtools/signing.py          @billmallard
/pyefis_data/cli.py            @billmallard
# The committed public keys.
/keys/                         @billmallard
# This file, so the rule cannot be removed without the review it enforces.
/.github/CODEOWNERS            @billmallard
